From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: with EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN or EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_COUNT=1, a refused allocation's report also names the deleted buffers still holding memory (EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS_DELETED); count only

What: BufferCache::ReportMemory (the port calls it from a refused allocation's report, after
EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS) adds one line: "EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS_DELETED <n> deleted buffers hold <MiB>
MiB, the largest <MiB> MiB; each goes 8 frame ends after its deletion" (a walk of
delayed_destruction_ring at that moment).
Why: at the load into the area past the field about 1.0-1.3 GB of the allocator's use is in no
report and no census field. If this line shows hundreds of MiB to 1 GB of deleted buffers at the
refusal, that is the unnamed memory, and 0801 is the fix; if it shows little, the unnamed memory
is something else (0731's allocator map then says what). With EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_COUNT=1 the
10 s line of 0801 also gives the peak of the same walk, before any refusal.
Off: one cached test at a refused allocation's report, nothing else.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 96b1a9710a..cf7092a3e2 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -142,6 +142,30 @@ void BufferCache<P>::ReportMemory() {
     std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS %zu buffers hold %llu MiB, the largest %llu MiB\n",
                  buffers, static_cast<unsigned long long>(total >> 20),
                  static_cast<unsigned long long>(largest >> 20));
+    // EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN=1|2 or EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_COUNT=1 (the same test as
+    // pressure_drain.h's GetMode): the deleted buffers still holding their memory
+    // (delayed_destruction_ring, freed TICKS_TO_DESTROY frame ends after their deletion, not when
+    // the GPU is done). No census field and no line above names them.
+    static const bool count_deleted = [] {
+        const char* const drain = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN");
+        const char* const count = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_COUNT");
+        return (drain != nullptr && (drain[0] == '1' || drain[0] == '2') && drain[1] == '\0') ||
+               (count != nullptr && count[0] == '1' && count[1] == '\0');
+    }();
+    if (count_deleted) {
+        size_t deleted{};
+        u64 deleted_bytes{}, deleted_largest{};
+        delayed_destruction_ring.ForEach([&](const Buffer& buffer) {
+            ++deleted;
+            deleted_bytes += buffer.SizeBytes();
+            deleted_largest = (std::max)(deleted_largest, u64{buffer.SizeBytes()});
+        });
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS_DELETED %zu deleted buffers hold %llu MiB, the largest "
+                     "%llu MiB; each goes %zu frame ends after its deletion\n",
+                     deleted, static_cast<unsigned long long>(deleted_bytes >> 20),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(deleted_largest >> 20), TICKS_TO_DESTROY);
+    }
 }
 
 template <class P>
